// Dogwood temporal policies - the refusal contract, enforced at the tool boundary.
//
// Dogwood is a strict superset of Cedar; every valid Cedar policy is valid
// Dogwood. It adds `formerly within`, `since within`, `count` and `sum`, which
// condition a decision on what the agent has ALREADY DONE in this session -
// scoped by the x-amzn-bedrock-agentcore-policy-session-id header.
//
// This is why the gate is a contract and not a suggestion: the model cannot
// talk its way past a policy that reasons over its own action history.

// 1. Advancing requires a passing gate observed in the last 20 seconds.
//    Not "the model believes it is ready" - an actual recent observation.
permit (
  principal,
  action == Action::"advance_step",
  resource
)
when {
  context.gate_passed formerly within 20 seconds
};

// 2. Alarm fatigue. Do not repeat the same refusal inside two minutes.
//    Every incumbent nags; a coach that repeats itself gets muted, and a muted
//    coach cannot warn you when it matters.
//
//    Scoped by VERDICT as well as by step. A repeated "not yet" must not spend
//    the budget a genuine "I can't tell" needs: suppressing a refusal down to a
//    wait would speak a readiness claim about a frame we declined to read.
//    Both stay visible on the panel either way - invariant 4.
forbid (
  principal,
  action == Action::"speak_refusal",
  resource
)
when {
  count(context.refusals_for_step_and_kind) >= 1 since within 120 seconds
};

// 3. Danger is never rate-limited and never gated on confidence.
//    A burning pan overrides every other rule in this file.
permit (
  principal,
  action == Action::"speak_abort",
  resource
);

// 4. Three corrections on the same step in one session means the threshold is
//    wrong, not the cook. Stop gating that step and hand control back.
//
//    The risk carve-out is load-bearing, not defensive. `forbid` beats `permit`
//    in Cedar and Dogwood, so without it this rule would forbid blocking an
//    advance over a burning pan - rule 3 permits `speak_abort`, a different
//    action, and would not save it. Invariant 3 outranks this rule.
//
//    Handing control back stops BLOCKING; it never claims readiness. The voice
//    still says "not yet" or "I can't tell", with "but it's your call" added.
forbid (
  principal,
  action == Action::"block_advance",
  resource
)
when {
  count(context.corrections_for_step) >= 3 since within 3600 seconds
  && context.risk != "urgent"
};
